      "message": "Serve the operator's door apart\n\nWhat grants access on a forge — registering people, handing out\nauthority, membership, stopping and restarting, quotas, the waitlist,\ninvitations, reports, mirrors and imports — can now be served on a\nloopback listener of its own, `--operator-listen`, and the public\nlistener refuses those paths whatever token comes with the request.\nMinting a token or setting a password for anybody but yourself is\nrefused there the same way. An admin token that travels through the\ntunnel opens nothing that grants access; the operator reaches the door\nover loopback, and everything else about the forge is the same on both\nlisteners. The flag takes only a loopback address, since that is the\npoint of it.\n\nBehind the door, four things a forge on its own may want: the waitlist\nto read and answer, an invitation by email that makes the account and\ntakes the address off the list, the reports to read and dismiss, and a\nswitch for strangers — `--open-signup` lets anyone make an account at\n/signup, rate limited by source, and off it says the forge takes people\nby invitation. The log records a self-made account as made by its\nowner. None of this knows about anything beyond one forge.\n\nAlso: a name reserved because a page lives there was checked in two\nplaces with two lists; it is one list again, with the two pages it had\nmissed. The fallback for an unknown API route named a document that\ndoes not exist; it names the ones that do.\n\nChange-Id: Ioperator0108\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
